<http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/systems/> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The System Capabilities Module imports SOSA and adds classes and properties required for the description of the operating conditions and capabilities of systems, particularly Sensors and Actuators."@en .
<http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/OperatingConditions> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/hasSystemCapability> <http://schema.org/domainIncludes> <http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Sensor> .
<http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/SuboptimalOperatingConditions> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/OperatingConditions> .
_:n14ebee0e8fd0426c9e58cb26ab513bccb1 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Agent> .
<http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/systems/> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2025-06-24"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/hasOperatingConditions> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/systems/> .
<http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/OperatingConditions> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "\n  Type of observation or observation collection that describe operating conditions of systems.\n  Sub-classes of this class explicit the desirability of the conditions.\n  Three such sub-classes are provided as a basic classification:\n  NormalOperatingConditions, SuboptimalOperatingConditions, and SurvivableConditions.\n  "@en .
<http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/systems/> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> _:n14ebee0e8fd0426c9e58cb26ab513bccb1 .
<http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/hasSystemCapability> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Relation between a System and an ObservationCollection (or Observation) describing the capability of the system. A sensor or system may have more than one set of system capabilities with different validity contexts."@en .
<http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/hasValidityContext> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Links a an observation collection or observation (typically about the system capabilities) or a property (typically about the system capabilities) to its validity context, described as an observation collection or observation (typically about the system environment)."@en .
<http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/SurvivableConditions> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "\n  Type of observation or observation collection that describe the conditions under which a system is expected to survive, that is to continue to exist in its current form,\n  even if its future operations are impaired. A typical example is the temperature at which a sensor looses physical integrity and looses its shape.\n  A system or sensor exposed to conditions outside of those reported by SurvivableConditions will no longer be serviceable.\n  "@en .
